#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:1
msgid ""
"This package parses [SPDX license expression](https://spdx.org/spdx-"
"specification-21-web-version#h.jxpfx0ykyb60) strings describing license "
"terms, like [package.json license "
"strings](https://docs.npmjs.com/files/package.json#license), into "
"consistently structured ECMAScript objects.  The npm command-line "
"interface depends on this package, as do many automatic license-audit "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:3
msgid "In a nutshell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:38
msgid ""
"The syntax comes from the [Software Package Data eXchange "
"(SPDX)](https://spdx.org/), a standard from the [Linux "
"Foundation](https://www.linuxfoundation.org) for shareable data about "
"software package license terms.  SPDX aims to make sharing and auditing "
"license data easy, especially for users of open-source software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:40
msgid ""
"The bulk of the SPDX standard describes syntax and semantics of XML "
"metadata files.  This package implements two lightweight, plain-text "
"components of that larger standard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:42
msgid ""
"The [license list](https://spdx.org/licenses), a mapping from specific "
"string identifiers, like `Apache-2.0`, to standard form license texts and"
" bolt-on license exceptions.  The [spdx-license-"
"ids](https://www.npmjs.com/package/spdx-license-ids) and [spdx-"
"exceptions](https://www.npmjs.com/package/spdx-exceptions) packages "
"implement the license list.  `spdx-expression-parse` depends on and "
"`require()`s them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:44
msgid ""
"Any license identifier from the license list is a valid license "
"expression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:56
msgid "So is any license identifier `WITH` a standardized license exception:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:69
msgid ""
"The license expression language, for describing simple and complex "
"license terms, like `MIT` for MIT-licensed and `(GPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0)` "
"for dual-licensing under GPL 2.0 and Apache 2.0.  `spdx-expression-parse`"
" itself implements license expression language, exporting a parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/spdx-expression-parse_README.md:91
msgid ""
"The Linux Foundation and its contributors license the SPDX standard under"
